title: Build property tests for numeric coercion
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: medium
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-04T05:31:38'
updated_at: '2026-06-13T07:48:19'
result: 'Added tests/coercion_property.rs: 6 proptest properties (64 cases each) covering
  int-var->f64-param (the historically-dropped case), int-literal->f64-param, int
  identity, int->f64 division, narrow-int->wider-int width coercion, and chained float
  coercion. Each compiles at both -O0 and -O3 and asserts equality with a Rust reference,
  catching -O-level mismatches and dropped coercions.'
description: 'Property tests for numeric coercion (review 07_type_system; relates
  to deleted auto-widen patch + MIR verifier). Current state: tests/proptest_smoke.rs
  only fuzzes lexer/parser never-panics; no numeric-coercion properties. The typer
  inserts explicit Cast nodes for mixed-width arithmetic (per A.2); MIR verifier (src/mir/verify.rs)
  enforces operand-type match. Deliverable: proptest suite generating random (value,
  src_type, dst_type, op) over i8..u64/f32/f64 asserting (1) compile-and-run result
  equals reference semantics computed in Rust (wrap/trap behavior per documented Jinn
  rules), (2) no UB/garbage on extremes (MIN/MAX, -1, 0), (3) cast round-trip laws
  where applicable. Definition of done: tests/numeric_coercion_property.rs in CI,
  documented coercion rules referenced (docs needed if rules undocumented — note in
  docs/ if missing).'
